                <h2>适用场景与前提条件</h2>
<p>本 SOP 适用于同时运营 Meta Business（Facebook/Instagram）、Google Ads、TikTok for Business 等多个海外广告平台的企业。如果你面临以下问题，这套流程会对你有帮助：</p>
<ul>
<li>各平台账单格式不一，汇总困难</li>
<li>充值金额与实际消耗存在差额，难以解释</li>
<li>发票认领滞后，影响成本核算</li>
<li>月底对账时间紧，容易出错</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>前提条件</strong>：确保已开通各平台的广告管理权限，并获取财务或充值后台的只读访问权限。</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>第一步：导出各平台充值记录</h2>
<h3>操作顺序</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>平台</th>
<th>充值记录导出路径</th>
<th>文件格式</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Meta Business</td>
<td>账单 → 付款记录 → 导出</td>
<td>CSV</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Google Ads</td>
<td>工具与设置 → 结算 → 交易记录</td>
<td>CSV/Excel</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>TikTok for Business</td>
<td>资产 → 账户账单 → 充值记录</td>
<td>Excel</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>执行要点</h3>
<ol>
<li>时间范围建议选取完整的自然月，便于与财务系统对齐</li>
<li>充值记录需包含：充值时间、充值金额、支付渠道、交易单号</li>
<li>如果通过第三方代理商充值，需额外记录代理商名称和付款凭证</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>第二步：导出各平台消耗报告</h2>
<p>消耗数据的导出优先级高于充值记录，因为消耗是实际发生的成本。</p>
<h3>推荐报告配置</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>维度</strong>：广告系列名称、广告组名称、受众定位</li>
<li><strong>指标</strong>：花费金额、展示次数、点击次数、转化次数</li>
<li><strong>时间分段</strong>：按天汇总（Daily）</li>
</ul>
<h3>注意事项</h3>
<p>部分平台的消耗数据存在 24-48 小时延迟，例如 Google Ads 的转化跟踪数据。导出后建议标记数据截止时间，避免使用不完整数据做判断。</p>
<hr />
<h2>第三步：汇总充值与消耗数据</h2>
<h3>基础汇总表模板字段</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>字段</th>
<th>来源</th>
<th>说明</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>平台名称</td>
<td>手动填写</td>
<td>Meta/Google/TikTok</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>账户 ID</td>
<td>从账单复制</td>
<td>避免仅用账户名称导致重名混淆</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>期间充值总额</td>
<td>第一步导出</td>
<td>本月所有充值相加</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>期间消耗总额</td>
<td>第二步导出</td>
<td>按消耗报告求和</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>期末余额</td>
<td>系统显示</td>
<td>或通过“充值-消耗”推算</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>发票金额</td>
<td>第四步填写</td>
<td>暂空</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>初判逻辑</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>充值 &gt; 消耗</strong>：正常情况，余额会结转下月</li>
<li><strong>充值 &lt; 消耗</strong>：可能是信用额度透支，或存在退款</li>
<li><strong>差异超过 5%</strong>：需进入第四步深度排查</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>第四步：认领与核对发票</h2>
<p>发票对账是很多团队容易忽略的环节。广告平台的发票通常有 1-2 周的延迟开具，与当月消耗存在时间差。</p>
<h3>发票认领流程</h3>
<ol>
<li>登录各平台后台，进入“账单”或“发票管理”模块</li>
<li>下载当月发票（PDF 或电子票）</li>
<li>在财务系统中匹配发票编号与充值记录</li>
<li>如果通过代理商充值，向代理商索取发票或对账函</li>
</ol>
<h3>常见问题处理</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>问题</th>
<th>解决方式</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>发票金额与充值金额不一致</td>
<td>检查是否有退款或余额抵扣</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>发票开具周期延迟</td>
<td>记录为“待认领”，次月初补齐</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>代理商发票晚于平台发票</td>
<td>以平台发票为准，代理商提供说明函</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>第五步：差异排查与调整</h2>
<p>完成基础汇总后，如果发现数据不一致，按以下顺序排查：</p>
<h3>排查清单</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] 充值记录是否完整？检查是否有漏掉的预付费充值</li>
<li>[ ] 消耗报告的时间范围是否与充值期间对齐？</li>
<li>[ ] 是否存在平台内部的余额转移或账户合并操作？</li>
<li>[ ] 货币兑换是否影响？非美元账户需确认汇率基准</li>
<li>[ ] 是否有人工调整或信贷额度使用？</li>
</ul>
<h3>调整操作规范</h3>
<p>对于无法解释的小额差异（通常在 0.1% 以内），建议记入“结算四舍五入差异”或“时区统计差异”科目，无需逐笔追溯。</p>
<hr />
<h2>第六步：输出对账报告与归档</h2>
<h3>报告必含内容</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>汇总表</strong>：各平台充值、消耗、余额、发票四列对比</li>
<li><strong>差异说明</strong>：如有差异需逐条说明原因</li>
<li><strong>责任人签字</strong>：运营负责人 + 财务负责人双签确认</li>
<li><strong>归档要求</strong>：原始账单、消耗报告、发票扫描件打包存储，建议保留 24 个月</li>
</ol>
<h3>常见对账周期</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>团队规模</th>
<th>推荐对账频率</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>初创团队（1-3 个账户）</td>
<td>每月一次，月中+月末</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>中型团队（5-10 个账户）</td>
<td>每周一次</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>规模化运营（10+ 账户）</td>
<td>每日自动对账，辅以周汇总</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>辅助工具推荐</h2>
<p>如果你的团队账户数量较多，建议使用以下工具提升效率：</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Google Sheets + 数据连接器</strong>：免费方案，适合中小团队</li>
<li><strong>Supermetrics / Windsor.ai</strong>：自动化拉取多平台消耗数据</li>
<li><strong>以渔数媒多账户管理后台</strong>：支持充值余额预警、统一账单导出</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>写在最后</h2>
<p>海外广告对账不是一次性工作，而是需要建立标准流程并持续执行的财务动作。建议在团队内部指定一名“财务对账负责人”，定期输出报告并同步给投放团队，让消耗数据与财务数据保持一致，为后续的 ROI 分析和预算分配提供可靠依据。</p>
            </div>
            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>When to Use This SOP</h2>
<p>This Standard Operating Procedure is designed for marketing teams and finance departments managing multiple overseas advertising platforms, including Meta Business (Facebook/Instagram), Google Ads, and TikTok for Business. Use this guide when facing:</p>
<ul>
<li>Inconsistent billing formats across platforms</li>
<li>Unclear discrepancies between recharge amounts and actual spend</li>
<li>Delayed invoice reconciliation affecting cost reporting</li>
<li>Time pressure during month-end closing</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Prerequisites</strong>: Ensure you have administrative access to ad accounts and read-only access to billing/recharge dashboards.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Export Recharge Records by Platform</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Platform</th>
<th>Export Path</th>
<th>Format</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Meta Business</td>
<td>Billing → Payment History → Export</td>
<td>CSV</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Google Ads</td>
<td>Tools &amp; Settings → Billing → Transactions</td>
<td>CSV/Excel</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>TikTok for Business</td>
<td>Assets → Account Billing → Recharge Records</td>
<td>Excel</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Key Actions</h3>
<ol>
<li>Select the full calendar month for alignment with financial systems</li>
<li>Include: recharge date, amount, payment method, transaction ID</li>
<li>For third-party agency recharges, record agency name and payment proof separately</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Export Spend Reports</h2>
<p>Spend data should be exported before recharge records, as spend represents actual cost.</p>
<h3>Recommended Report Configuration</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Dimensions</strong>: Campaign name, Ad group, Audience targeting</li>
<li><strong>Metrics</strong>: Amount spent, Impressions, Clicks, Conversions</li>
<li><strong>Time Breakdown</strong>: Daily aggregation</li>
</ul>
<h3>Note on Data Delay</h3>
<p>Some platforms have 24-48 hour delays on conversion data (e.g., Google Ads). Mark the data cutoff time after export to avoid using incomplete figures.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Consolidate Recharge and Spend Data</h2>
<h3>Basic Summary Table Fields</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Field</th>
<th>Source</th>
<th>Notes</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Platform</td>
<td>Manual entry</td>
<td>Meta/Google/TikTok</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Account ID</td>
<td>From billing</td>
<td>Use ID, not name, to avoid duplicates</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Monthly Recharge Total</td>
<td>Step 1</td>
<td>Sum all recharges</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Monthly Spend Total</td>
<td>Step 2</td>
<td>Sum from spend reports</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Ending Balance</td>
<td>System display</td>
<td>Or calculate: Recharge - Spend</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Invoice Amount</td>
<td>Step 4</td>
<td>Leave blank for now</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Initial Assessment</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Recharge &gt; Spend</strong>: Normal, balance rolls over</li>
<li><strong>Recharge &lt; Spend</strong>: Possible credit usage or refunds</li>
<li><strong>Variance &gt; 5%</strong>: Proceed to Step 5 for investigation</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Invoice Claim and Verification</h2>
<p>Invoice reconciliation is often overlooked. Ad platforms typically issue invoices 1-2 weeks after month-end.</p>
<h3>Invoice Claim Workflow</h3>
<ol>
<li>Access the billing/invoice module in each platform</li>
<li>Download monthly invoices (PDF or e-invoice)</li>
<li>Match invoice numbers with recharge records in financial system</li>
<li>For agency recharges, request invoices or reconciliation letters</li>
</ol>
<h3>Common Issue Resolution</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Issue</th>
<th>Solution</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Invoice amount differs from recharge</td>
<td>Check for refunds or balance deductions</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Invoice delay</td>
<td>Mark as "Pending" and complete next month</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Agency invoice later than platform</td>
<td>Use platform invoice as primary, require agency explanation letter</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Step 5: Variance Investigation and Adjustment</h2>
<p>After consolidation, investigate discrepancies with this checklist:</p>
<h3>Investigation Checklist</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Are all recharge records complete? Check for missing prepaid recharges</li>
<li>[ ] Does the spend report date range align with the recharge period?</li>
<li>[ ] Any internal balance transfers or account mergers?</li>
<li>[ ] Currency conversion impact? Verify exchange rate basis for non-USD accounts</li>
<li>[ ] Any manual adjustments or credit line usage?</li>
</ul>
<h3>Adjustment Guidelines</h3>
<p>For unexplainable minor variances (typically under 0.1%), record as "Rounding Difference" or "Time Zone Statistical Variance" — no need to trace every cent.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 6: Output Reconciliation Report and Archive</h2>
<h3>Report Must Include</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Summary Table</strong>: Four-column comparison per platform (recharge, spend, balance, invoice)</li>
<li><strong>Variance Explanation</strong>: Document each discrepancy with cause</li>
<li><strong>Sign-off</strong>: Operations lead + Finance lead dual approval</li>
<li><strong>Archiving</strong>: Package original statements, spend reports, invoice scans; retain for 24 months minimum</li>
</ol>
<h3>Recommended Reconciliation Frequency</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Team Size</th>
<th>Frequency</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Startup (1-3 accounts)</td>
